OL,3,GNEWSADivers explore mysteries of 14th
OL,4,ACentury lost town
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe remains of a Norfolk town that was
OL,7,Fclaimed by the sea about 700 years ago
OL,8,Fhave been explored by divers in an
OL,9,Fattempt to map its seabed site.
OL,11,FShipden once graced the north Norfolk
OL,12,Fcoast until it appeared to succumb to
OL,13,Fthe waves in the 14th Century - with
OL,14,Fits demise shrouded in myth and
OL,15,Fspeculation.
OL,17,FDivers explored an area off Cromer and
OL,18,Fphotographed 25 manmade features - but
OL,19,Ffound no trace of a church which,
OL,20,Faccording to legend, had a bell that
OL,21,Fcould be heard tolling from the depths.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
